---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import EqBars from "../../components/EqBars.astro";
import { insiderHref } from "../../lib/insiderLink";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About WAG Podcast"
  description="What WAG Podcast actually is: a weekly, video-first talk show hosted by three teen girls, its format, its topics, and how it fits into The Wild Adventure Girls."
  ogImage="/images/studio/wag-studio-428.jpg"
>
  <section class="about-hero">
    <div class="hero-photo">
      <picture>
        <source srcset="/images/studio/wag-studio-428.webp" type="image/webp" />
        <img src="/images/studio/wag-studio-428.jpg" alt="Angelina, Scarlett, and Annabella backstage at the WAG Podcast studio" fetchpriority="high" />
      </picture>
      <div class="hero-scrim"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="container hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow"><EqBars size="sm" /> About</p>
      <h1>What WAG Podcast <span class="text-accent">actually</span> is.</h1>
      <p class="lede">The show, the format, and how it fits into the wider Wild Adventure Girls world.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-body">
    <div class="container" data-reveal="stagger">
      <div class="about-block">
        <h2>A weekly, unscripted talk show</h2>
        <p>WAG Podcast is a weekly video podcast hosted by Angelina, Scarlett, and Annabella. Every episode is filmed in their own studio — no writers' room, no script. It's the same real dynamic the three of them have off camera, just with a mic on: trending topics, viral dares, fan questions, and the kind of behind-the-scenes stories that don't make it into a normal video.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-block">
        <h2>Video-first, not audio-only</h2>
        <p>Most podcasts are built for audio and treat video as an afterthought. WAG Podcast is the opposite — full episodes are shot for YouTube first, then released as audio-only versions on Spotify and Apple Podcasts for anyone who'd rather just listen. If you've never watched a <a href="/video-podcasts-for-teens/">video podcast built for teens</a> before, this is built to be watched.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-photo-break">
        <picture>
          <source srcset="/images/studio/wag-studio-283.webp" type="image/webp" />
          <img src="/images/studio/wag-studio-283.jpg" alt="Angelina, Scarlett, and Annabella recording WAG Podcast" loading="lazy" />
        </picture>
      </div>

      <div class="about-block">
        <h2>What topics come up</h2>
        <p>There's no fixed theme episode to episode — that's on purpose, since real conversations don't work that way. Recurring territory includes trending topics and pop culture, friendship and relationship questions, real talk about tough stuff, party games and challenges, the actual chaos of <a href="/topics/growing-up/">growing up</a>, and behind-the-scenes stories from filming Wild Adventure Girls content. It's also, honestly, a <a href="/teen-comedy-podcast/">pretty funny</a> way to spend twenty minutes.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-block">
        <h2>How it relates to The Wild Adventure Girls</h2>
        <p>WAG Podcast is published by <a href="https://wildadventuregirls.com/">The Wild Adventure Girls</a> — the teen entertainment brand Angelina, Scarlett, and Annabella built on YouTube making adventure, mystery-investigation, and challenge content. The podcast is a separate show with its own format and its own weekly release, not a repackaged version of that content. Full episode-by-episode coverage — every episode's own page, topic hubs, and companion articles — lives on the main WAG site; this site is the show's own home.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-block">
        <h2>Who's behind it</h2>
        <p>Angelina, Scarlett, and Annabella are real sisters and a cousin, not a cast brought together for a show. <a href="/hosts/">Meet the hosts →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-cta">
    <div class="container">
      <a class="btn btn-accent" href="/watch/">Watch an Episode →</a>
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/listen/">Listen Now →</a>
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/faq/">FAQ →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="join">
    <div class="container register-light join-inner" data-reveal>
      <h2>Never miss a new episode.</h2>
      <p>Join WAG Insider for new-episode alerts and behind-the-scenes extras — the same free list the main WAG site uses, one signup for everything WAG.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={insiderHref("about")}>Join WAG Insider →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero{ position:relative; padding: 0 0 32px; }
  .hero-photo{ position:relative; width:100%; aspect-ratio: 2.6/1; overflow:hidden; margin-bottom:40px; }
  .hero-photo img{ width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover; object-position: center 30%; display:block; }
  .hero-scrim{ position:absolute; inset:0; background: linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(10,10,15,.75) 0%, transparent 45%); }
  .hero-inner{ max-width:68ch; }
  .eyebrow{ display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:10px; }
  .about-hero h1{ font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.2vw, 3.1rem); max-width:20ch; }
  .text-accent{
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--wag-pink) 0%, var(--wag-green) 100%);
    -webkit-background-clip:text; background-clip:text; color:transparent;
  }
  .lede{ font-size:1.1rem; max-width:60ch; }

  .about-body{ padding: 48px 0; }
  .about-block{
    max-width:70ch; margin-bottom:28px; padding:24px 28px; border-radius: var(--radius);
    border:1px solid transparent; transition: border-color .2s ease, background .2s ease;
  }
  .about-block:hover{ border-color: var(--line); background: var(--bg-alt); }
  .about-block h2{ font-size:1.3rem; margin-bottom:.5em; }
  .about-block p{ font-size:1rem; }
  .about-block a{ color: var(--wag-green); font-weight:600; text-decoration:underline; }

  .about-photo-break{
    max-width:70ch; margin: 8px 0 36px; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); overflow:hidden;
    border: 2px solid transparent;
    background:
      linear-gradient(var(--bg), var(--bg)) padding-box,
      linear-gradient(120deg, var(--wag-pink), var(--wag-green)) border-box;
  }
  .about-photo-break img{ width:100%; aspect-ratio: 16/9; object-fit:cover; object-position: center 30%; display:block; }

  .about-cta{ padding: 8px 0 40px; display:flex; gap:16px; flex-wrap:wrap; border-top:1px solid var(--line); padding-top:40px; }
  .btn-outline{ border-color: var(--ink); }
  .btn-outline:hover{ background: var(--ink); color: var(--bg); }

  .join{ padding: 8px 0 72px; }
  .join-inner{
    padding:44px 40px; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); text-align:center;
    display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center; gap:14px;
    position:relative;
    background:
      linear-gradient(var(--bg), var(--bg)) padding-box,
      linear-gradient(120deg, var(--wag-pink), var(--wag-green)) border-box;
    border: 2px solid transparent;
  }
  .join-inner h2{ font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.8vw, 2rem); margin:0; }
  .join-inner p{ max-width:52ch; margin:0; }
</style>
